# Own-wording spells of Grim Hollow Player's Guide (2014 rules), part B.
HL = "\n\n**At Higher Levels.** "
TEXT = {
"Investiture of Venom": ["Self, 10 minutes, Concentration. Immune to Poison and the Poisoned condition. Strip poison defenses and spray a 4d6 Poison line.",
 "Self, up to 10 minutes, Concentration. Your veins turn green and your eyes weep poison. For the duration: you are immune to Poison damage and the Poisoned condition. When you pick a creature you see within 30 ft, you know if it resists or is immune to Poison or the Poisoned condition. As a bonus action you can choose a creature within 30 ft. It makes a Constitution save or loses any Poison resistance or immunity and immunity to the Poisoned condition until the end of your next turn. As an action you can spray toxins in a line 15 ft long and 5 ft wide. Each creature in it makes a Constitution save, taking 4d6 Poison damage on a failure and half on a success. A creature that fails is also Poisoned until the end of your next turn."],
"Little Death": ["Self, up to 8 hours, Concentration. You die and rise as a ghost. You return to life if your token stays on your corpse.",
 "Self, up to 8 hours, Concentration. You drop to 0 hit points and die. At the start of your next turn you become a ghost in your corpse's space, using the ghost's statistics but keeping your alignment and personality. You can use only the ghost's abilities. You add your Proficiency Bonus to your ghost attack rolls and to the save DCs of your ghost abilities. The DM secretly rolls 1d8 when you cast it. After that many hours the spell ends. It ends early if you drop to 0 hit points as a ghost or choose to end it with an action. If the material component is still on your corpse, you return to life with half your hit point maximum. If not, you make death saves as normal. If your body is destroyed or ruined while the spell is active, the duration becomes indefinite and you stay a ghost until you drop to 0 hit points, are destroyed another way, or your body is hit by an effect that kills the living, such as raise dead or resurrection."],
"Magic Mirror": ["Self, instant, reaction when targeted by a spell. Redirect the spell to a creature you see within 60 ft.",
 "Self, instant. You take this reaction when a spell targets you. A bubble of shimmering energy forms between you and the caster. The spell is redirected to a creature of your choice that you see within 60 ft. If the spell is 5th level or lower, you stop being a target and the chosen creature becomes one. If it is 6th level or higher, make an ability check with your spellcasting ability against DC 10 plus the spell's level. On a success the spell is redirected as above. On a failure you stay the target."],
"Mortality": ["120 ft, 1 minute, Concentration. Spend five Hit Dice. A celestial, elemental, fey, aberration or fiend loses hit points and becomes mortal.",
 "120 ft, up to 1 minute, Concentration. You must spend five Hit Dice to cast this, or the spell fails. Choose an aberration, celestial, elemental, fey or fiend in range. It makes a Charisma save or has its current and maximum hit points reduced by the total of the dice. For the duration, a creature that fails also loses all damage immunities and resistances, becomes a humanoid, and takes an extra 1d4 Necrotic damage each time it takes damage. If it drops to 0 hit points under the spell, the changes become permanent and it dies. Only restoring it to life and casting remove curse or similar magic reverses that."],
"Neutralize Aura": ["Touch, 1 hour, Concentration. A willing creature cannot be magically sensed by fey, fiends, celestials or undead.",
 "Touch, up to 1 hour, Concentration. You mask the aura of a willing creature. For the duration, fey, fiends, celestials and undead cannot perceive it by magic. The spell ends if the creature attacks, casts a spell, deals damage, takes damage, or steps within 5 ft of one of those creatures." + HL + "Target one more creature for each slot level above 1st."],
"Phoenix Flames": ["Self, instant. Holy fire erupts in a 20-ft radius for 30d6 Radiant and exhaustion. You rise again after 10 minutes.",
 "Self, instant. You burn yourself away in a cloud of holy flames. Each creature within 20 ft makes a Constitution save, taking 30d6 Radiant damage and gaining one level of exhaustion on a failure, or half damage and no exhaustion on a success. A creature killed by this damage is incinerated. After 10 minutes you rise from the ashes where you cast it, fully restored as if by true resurrection."],
"Reanimate": ["Touch, instant. Spend three Hit Dice to raise a creature dead under 10 minutes with 1 hit point and a burst of vigor.",
 "Touch, instant. You must spend three Hit Dice to cast this, or the spell fails. Touch a creature that died in the last 10 minutes. It returns to life with 1 hit point. Roll the spent dice and it gains that many temporary hit points. At the start of each of its turns it loses 1 of these. While it has any, it gets +2 to all ability checks, attack rolls and saves. When they are gone, it gains one level of exhaustion. The spell cannot raise a creature that died of old age or restore missing body parts."],
"Red Rain": ["Self, 8 hours, Concentration, 10-minute cast. Spend eight Hit Dice. Blood rain over 5 miles exhausts and harms creatures and blights the land.",
 "Self, up to 8 hours, Concentration, casting time 10 minutes. You must spend eight Hit Dice to cast this, or the spell fails. Over the next 1d6 x 5 minutes the sky darkens and blood rains over everything within 5 miles of you. A creature directly exposed gains one level of exhaustion every 10 minutes. Each time it gains a level this way it takes 2d10 Necrotic damage and its hit point maximum drops by the same amount until it is no longer exhausted. While it has any exhaustion from this spell it automatically fails saves against being Poisoned or diseased. Beast and plant creatures in the area make a Wisdom save or are Frightened until they spend 1 minute outside the area. Ordinary plants wither and die after 10 minutes of exposure. For each hour you keep concentrating, roll one of the spent dice. At the end, the total is the number of days before beasts willingly return and plants regrow in the area."],
"Ride the Lightning": ["Self, instant. Become lightning and teleport up to 60 ft. Creatures within 5 ft of the path take 4d6 Lightning damage.",
 "Self, instant. You turn into a bolt of lightning and teleport up to 60 ft to an open space you see. Each creature within 5 ft of the line between your start and end points takes 4d6 Lightning damage." + HL + "The damage rises by 1d6 and the distance by 10 ft for each slot level above 4th."],
"Sanguine Poppet": ["Touch, 1 hour, Concentration, 1-minute cast. Spend three Hit Dice to animate a figure you can scout through or detonate.",
 "Touch, up to 1 hour, Concentration, casting time 1 minute. You must spend three Hit Dice to cast this, or the spell fails. You smear a creature-shaped object with your blood and it becomes your sanguine poppet. Its AC is 10 plus your Proficiency Bonus plus your spellcasting modifier, and it has 30 hit points. If it drops to 0 or is more than a mile from you, the spell ends. As a bonus action it can walk or climb 30 ft, and you see and hear through it until the start of your next turn. As an action you can make it burst in a spray of blood and end the spell. Roll the spent dice. Each creature within 30 ft makes a Constitution save, taking Necrotic damage equal to the total on a failure and half on a success." + HL + "Spend one more Hit Die for each slot level above 3rd. The duration also rises by 1 hour per level above 3rd."],
"Sanguine Shield": ["Self, 1 minute, Concentration. Spend two Hit Dice. Gain 5 temporary hit points per wounded creature within 30 ft (max 15) and half cover from ranged attacks.",
 "Self, up to 1 minute, Concentration. You must spend two Hit Dice to cast this, or the spell fails. You draw life from the wounded around you into a swirling shield of blood. You gain 5 temporary hit points for each creature within 30 ft that is below its hit point maximum, you included, up to 15. While you have them, you have half cover against ranged attacks. When the spell ends you lose any left." + HL + "The maximum rises by 5 for every two slot levels above 2nd."],
"Sense Lifeblood": ["Self, 1 minute, Concentration. Spend two Hit Dice. Sense kinship and who is at half hit points or less, and deal bonus damage to them.",
 "Self, up to 1 minute, Concentration. You must spend two Hit Dice to cast this, or the spell fails. You sense the lifeblood of creatures you see. For the duration you can tell whether and how two or more creatures you see are related by blood. You also know whether a creature's hit points are at or below half. When you damage such a creature, you roll the two spent dice as extra damage." + HL + "A 4th or 5th level slot lets you concentrate for up to 1 hour. A 6th level or higher slot lets you concentrate for up to 8 hours."],
"Serpent Tongue": ["Self, 1 minute. Your tongue becomes a serpent that bites for 1d8 Piercing and can Poison. Bonus action to repeat.",
 "Self, 1 minute. Your tongue becomes a venomous snake. When you cast it, make a melee spell attack against a creature within 5 ft. On a hit the target takes 1d8 Piercing damage and makes a Constitution save or is Poisoned. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the condition on a success. As a bonus action on your turn you can attack again against a creature within 5 ft." + HL + "The damage rises by 1d8 for each slot level above 3rd."],
"Spirit Swarm": ["120 ft, 1 minute, Concentration. Charisma save or 8d8 Psychic damage and Frightened of you. Half damage and no fear on a success.",
 "120 ft, up to 1 minute, Concentration. You call spirits to avenge themselves on a creature you see in range. It makes a Charisma save. A creature with Charisma 2 or lower is immune. On a failure the target takes 8d8 Psychic damage and is Frightened of you until the spell ends. On a success it takes half damage and is not Frightened."],
"Steal Immortality": ["300 ft, instant, reaction. Spend nine Hit Dice to kill a downed celestial, elemental, fey, fiend or undead and take its nature.",
 "300 ft, instant. You take this reaction when a celestial, elemental, fey, fiend or undead you see in range drops to 0 hit points. You must spend nine Hit Dice to cast it, or the spell fails. Roll them and note the total as your mortal hit points. The triggering creature dies at once, and is destroyed if it would normally return to its home plane. Your creature type becomes that of the dead creature. While changed you are immune to Poison damage and disease, need no food, drink or air, and resist nonmagical damage. You also gain a benefit by type. Celestial: Resistance to Radiant and Necrotic damage and a fly speed of 60 ft. Elemental: Resistance to Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning and Thunder damage. Fey: as a bonus action on each of your turns you turn invisible until the start of your next turn or teleport up to 60 ft. Fiend: Resistance to Cold and Fire damage and a fly speed of 60 ft. Undead: immunity to Necrotic damage and to being Charmed or Frightened. You keep the type until you cast this spell again, which ends the old effects, or until you drop to 0 hit points, which returns your type to normal and your hit points to your mortal hit points."],
"Suffocate": ["60 ft, 1 minute, Concentration. Spell attack to Restrain a creature with invisible hands. Creatures that need air begin to suffocate.",
 "60 ft, up to 1 minute, Concentration. You form a pair of grasping hands of invisible force. Make a spell attack against a creature you see in range. On a hit it is Restrained as the hands crush its throat or equivalent. If it needs air, it starts to suffocate. A suffocating creature survives a number of rounds equal to 1 plus its Constitution modifier (minimum 1). At the start of its next turn after that, it becomes Unconscious and cannot regain hit points until it can breathe. A conscious restrained creature can use its action to make a Strength or Dexterity check (its choice) against your spell save DC. On a success the spell ends on it."],
"Supernal Smite": ["Self, 1 minute, Concentration, bonus action. Your next melee hit deals 4d6 Force damage and strips magic from the target.",
 "Self, up to 1 minute, Concentration. The next time you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack during the spell, your weapon shatters the magic around it. The attack deals an extra 4d6 Force damage. If the creature is concentrating, its concentration breaks. Any spell of 3rd level or lower on it ends. For each spell of 4th level or higher on it, make an ability check with your spellcasting ability against DC 10 plus that spell's level. On a success the spell ends."],
"Theft of Vitae": ["Self, instant, reaction when a creature within 30 ft takes damage. Spend two Hit Dice to deal Necrotic damage and gain temporary hit points (max 25).",
 "Self, instant. You take this reaction when a creature you see within 30 ft takes damage. You must spend two Hit Dice to cast it, or the spell fails. Roll them. The creature takes that much Necrotic damage. You then gain temporary hit points equal to the triggering damage plus this Necrotic damage, up to 25." + HL + "The maximum rises by 10 for each slot level above 2nd."],
"Wall of Gloom": ["120 ft, 10 minutes, Concentration. A grey wall of sorrow blocks sight and incapacitates nearby creatures that fail Charisma saves.",
 "120 ft, up to 10 minutes, Concentration. You raise a wall of swirling grey energy made of the pain of loss on a solid surface in range. It is up to 60 ft long, 10 ft high and 5 ft thick, or a circle with a 20-ft diameter, up to 20 ft high and 5 ft thick. It blocks line of sight and sheds dim light out to 100 ft. You and creatures you name when you cast it can pass through and stay near it unharmed. Another creature that moves within 20 ft of it, or starts its turn there, makes a Charisma save or is Incapacitated for a round by a flood of despair. A creature can pass through the wall, but it is draining. The first time a creature enters the wall on a turn, or ends its turn in it, it makes a Charisma save or gains one level of exhaustion."],
"Wilting Smite": ["Self, 1 minute, Concentration, bonus action. Spend two Hit Dice. Your next melee hit deals extra Necrotic damage and removes resistances.",
 "Self, up to 1 minute, Concentration. You must spend two Hit Dice to cast this, or the spell fails. The next time you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack during the spell, blood runs over your weapon and dries to black spores. Roll the spent dice. The attack deals that much extra Necrotic damage. The creature also loses all damage resistances until the start of your next turn."],
"Wrack": ["30 ft, 1 minute, Concentration. Constitution save or painful spasms halve speed and impose Disadvantage on attacks.",
 "30 ft, up to 1 minute, Concentration. Choose a creature you see in range. It makes a Constitution save or is wracked with muscle spasms for the duration. It has half speed and Disadvantage on attack rolls. At the end of each of its turns it makes another Wisdom save, ending the spell on itself on a success."],
}
